{"kind":"request","text":"Converge the three binaries' resident-HTTP and submit plumbing into one shared internal client package, closing the unguarded gap in gitseq-github.\n\nEvidence (verified at main 88b51864; re-verify every citation at the implementation head): the bounded, no-redirect, strict-JSON transport exists in five variants (cmd/gs/main.go:1378-1416 getJSON; cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:1017-1062 postBoundedJSON, 1064-1100 getBoundedJSON, 1102-1131 do). The loopback-URL guard is duplicated (cmd/gs/main.go:1361-1376 and 1590-1603; cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:1191-1205) and entirely absent from cmd/gitseq-github/main.go:244, which posts to /v0/submit with a bare http.Post — no loopback, redirect, or response-size guard. Local-vs-resident submission is triplicated (cmd/gs/main.go:1271-1292; cmd/gitseq-github/main.go:232-260; cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:813-834), each decoding the same anonymous struct{app.Submission; Error string} envelope above the single owner app.AcceptSubmission (internal/app/app.go:794). The undefined-kind warning (cmd/gs/main.go:1260-1269 vs cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:841-858) and GITSEQ_ACTOR resolution (cmd/gs/main.go:43-63 vs cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:215-227) ride along in duplicate. Only MCP consults ResidentURL discovery (internal/app/resident.go:55); gs and the connector make the operator re-supply the URL by flag.\n\nDirection: one package (e.g. internal/residentclient or app/client) owning URL validation, the bounded transport, and Submit(ctx, workspace, serverURL, request); the three binaries keep only their routing policy (gs: flag; mcp: resident-first fallback; connector: flag). This centralizes the existing checks — it does not implement the new supported-host authorization policy that the open P1 architecture request covers, but it creates the single place where that policy will later land. Do not weaken any existing guard.","body":{"conditions":"One internal package owns loopback-URL validation, the bounded no-redirect strict-JSON round-trip, and resident-or-local Submit; cmd/gs, cmd/gitseq-mcp, and cmd/gitseq-github all consume it; gitseq-github gains the same guard the others have; kind-warning and GITSEQ_ACTOR resolution are shared; observable transport behavior otherwise unchanged; make test and make race pass; implemented on a request/ branch, reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 88b51864; only AGENTS.md/SKILL.md changed through 6b69288d; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}